  "scientific_conclusion": "Under strictly subject/finger-disjoint 5-fold cross-validation on real fingerprints from DB1_B, both Logistic Regression and Random Forest confirm that 9-D Pure Geometric descriptors eliminate direct minutiae-type coordinate storage (0 binary variables stored). Empirical inferential attacks achieve only 52.10% (LR) and 50.84% (RF) balanced accuracy, while protected 32-bit templates achieve 51.57% (LR) and 51.29% (RF). After Benjamini-Hochberg FDR control (m=2 family), residual inferential leakage remains tightly bounded near uninformative chance (50.0%), confirming robust privacy preservation against attribute inference."
